Third-party software:

This product depends on software distributed under separate, compatible
open-source licenses. Each dependency retains its own license; the applicable
license and copyright are in that package's own metadata and license file.

Distributed builds carry the runtime dependencies with them, so those licenses
travel with the build. Assembling them into one attribution list that ships with
the application is tracked as an open item, not something this file claims is
already done.

Corral integrates with third-party AI providers, trackers, and repositories
using credentials supplied by the user (BYOK). Corral does not bundle any
proprietary provider binary, and does not embed any provider credentials.
Compliance with each provider's terms of service is the user's responsibility.
